GS diagnostics and queue-record guards: one TSC-to-ns calibration, a non-underflowing `[gs-fe] other`, and
rejection of truncated records before they are read

`gs_frontend.cpp` and `gs_threaded_backend.cpp` each calibrated their own `nsPerTick` (a third copy lives in the
`[gs-pub]` reporter), so two counters printed in the same 5 s window were not necessarily comparable. The new
`gs_diag_clock.h` owns the calibration and the 5 s report window; both reporters use it and keep their one-shot sample
in a function-local static, so the per-vertex path pays no extra cost.

`[gs-fe] other` was `all - build - submit` on unsigned ticks: nested sampling (or a counter reset mid-window) made it
underflow to a huge value. It is now clamped to 0, with the counter contract written where the counters are added.
The two `Op::Run` drop modes are stated at `reportRunAnomaly`.

`GSThreadedBackend::Execute` read a full `LoadClut`/`Submit`/`WriteVram`/`Sync`/`Present` struct from a record whose
length field could be shorter than the struct, consuming the following record's bytes. A per-op `minimumPayload` table
now checks the framed length before any read; a short record is reported, counted in `run_drops` and skipped while the
rest of the chunk stays framed. `Op::Run` keeps its own n-dependent check; its `length < 4u` + `break` became
`continue`, which only makes the existing control flow explicit.

Measured with patch 90 in the same binary: A/B, Asia disc, ship deck, 0.5x, 63 s, base/final alternating (four runs),
t=50-60 s: `vu_ms` 4634.96 -> 4651.29 (+0.35 %, inside the +/-1 % band), `gs_ms` 2504.9 -> 2323.7, `anomalies=0`,
`run_drops=0 run_overflows=0`, `levelReady=1`.

